cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite AperiTrace if you use this software."
type: software
title: "AperiTrace: Event-resolved membership analysis and finite diffraction for cut-and-project models"
version: "0.1.0"
authors:
  - family-names: Lee
    given-names: Myungin
    email: myungin@umd.edu
    affiliation: "College of Computer, Mathematical, and Natural Sciences, University of Maryland, College Park, MD, USA"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  AperiTrace is implemented as the Python package qc5d.
  Linked Python inspection retains exact five-integer lattice identity across
  physical projection, linear-offset selection history, finite diffraction,
  and independently recomputable exports in a canonical finite decagonal model.
keywords:
  - cut-and-project
  - quasicrystals
  - finite diffraction
  - scientific software
